//! The `rotate` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property allows you to
//! specify rotation transforms individually and independently of the `transform` property. This maps
//! better to typical user interface usage, and saves having to remember the exact order of transform
//! functions to specify in the `transform` property.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: Specifies that no rotation should be applied.
//!
//! Grammar: none | <angle> | [ x | y | z | <number>{3} ] && <angle>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transforms-2/#propdef-rotate
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/rotate
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

